<title>HONG KONG: Harbin Power posts lower interim profit.</title>
<headline>Harbin Power posts lower interim profit.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended June 30</p>
<p>(in million yuan unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (yuan)		   0.0274 vs 0.0464</p>
<p>    Dividend (yuan)	    nil    vs 0.015</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil    vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    32.61  vs 55.18</p>
<p>    Turnover		     916.13 vs 1,229.99</p>
<p>    Company name		 Harbin Power Equipment Co Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  N/A</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Harbin Power, one of China's largest power equipment makers, said the lowering of the export value added tax rebate to nine percent from 14 percent with effect from January 1, 1996 had cut its profit by 2.8 million yuan.</p>
<p>-- HK Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
